---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="40–45 min" data-extension-duration="10–15 min">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 05</p>
  <h1>Regular <em>plural</em> nouns</h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Exactly one thing usually takes a singular noun: <span class="ex">one client</span>. Zero or a number greater than one takes a plural noun: <span class="ex">zero clients, two clients</span>. This lesson teaches the most useful regular spelling patterns: <span class="ex">-s</span>, <span class="ex">-es</span>, and <span class="ex">-ies</span>.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">40–45 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">-s / -es / -ies</span>
    <span class="tag">one / zero / many</span>
    <span class="tag">10–15 min optional practice</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Compare book, watch, and city.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Look at the last letters.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Match, choose, and build plurals.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Count the things in your real life.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Use these patterns with <strong>countable nouns</strong>, things you can count as one, two, or three: <span class="ex">one office, two offices</span>. Use a plural noun after <strong>zero</strong>, after numbers greater than one, and with <span class="ex">these / those</span>: <span class="ex">zero emails, three emails, these keys</span>.</p>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h2>Retrieve what you know</h2>
    <p>Say the missing words before you continue.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Exactly one: <span class="ex">___ client</span>. Possible answers: <span class="ex">a client</span> or <span class="ex">one client</span>.</li>
      <li>More than one and near you: <span class="ex">___ clients</span>. Answer: <span class="ex">these clients</span>.</li>
      <li>What changes between <span class="ex">one phone</span> and <span class="ex">two phones</span>?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>One, then many</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">one book → two books &nbsp; · &nbsp; one watch → two watches &nbsp; · &nbsp; one city → two cities</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>What do we add to <span class="ex">book</span> to make it plural? Look at the end of the word.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">watch</span> does not just add <span class="ex">-s</span>. What did we add instead? Why might that be easier to say?</li>
      <li><span class="ex">city</span> changes the last letter before <span class="ex">-es</span>. What letter disappears, and what replaces it?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. Client takes -s, box and class take -es, and company changes consonant + y to -ies.">
    <h3>Discovery check: read the ending, then choose</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Look at the last letters of the singular word in brackets</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="-s" data-value-label-variant="token">add -s</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="-es" data-value-label-variant="token">add -es</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="-ies" data-value-label-variant="token">change y to -ies</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="-s" data-hint="Client does not end in s, x, z, ch, sh, or consonant + y." data-fix="client + -s → clients" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(client → client__)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="-es" data-hint="Box ends in -x, one of the endings that needs an extra written e." data-fix="box + -es → boxes" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(box → box__, ends in -x)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="-ies" data-hint="Company ends in a consonant followed by y." data-fix="company: drop y, add -ies → companies" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(company → compan__, consonant + y)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="-es" data-hint="Class ends in an s sound and needs an extra syllable in the plural." data-fix="class + -es → classes" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(class → class__, ends in -ss)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: four spelling decisions</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>First decide whether the noun is countable and whether the meaning is exactly one or not one. Then look at the <strong>last letters</strong> of a regular countable noun.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>The word ends in…</th><th>add</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>most letters</td><td><b>-s</b></td><td><span class="contraction">book → books · phone → phones · client → clients</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>-s, -x, -z, -ch, -sh</b></td><td><b>-es</b></td><td><span class="contraction">bus → buses · box → boxes · watch → watches · dish → dishes · class → classes</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>consonant + y</b></td><td><b>-ies</b> <span class="contraction">(drop the y)</span></td><td><span class="contraction">city → cities · company → companies · country → countries</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>vowel + y</b></td><td><b>-s</b> <span class="contraction">(keep the y)</span></td><td><span class="contraction">day → days · key → keys · boy → boys</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Where these regular rules stop</h3>
    <p>These patterns cover many common regular nouns, but not every English plural. Some common nouns change differently: <span class="ex">person → people, child → children, man → men, woman → women</span>. Words ending in <span class="ex">-o</span> or <span class="ex">-f / -fe</span> do not all follow one safe spelling rule, so check a dictionary when you are unsure. For example, <span class="ex">photo → photos</span>, but <span class="ex">tomato → tomatoes</span>.</p>
    <p>One final <span class="ex">z</span> often doubles before <span class="ex">-es</span>: <span class="ex">quiz → quizzes</span>. Learn this spelling with the word.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Pronunciation focus: say the plural ending</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The written ending is not always the spoken sound. Listen to the final sound in the singular noun, then move smoothly into the plural ending.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>You hear at the end</th><th>Plural sound</th><th>Say it</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>a quiet, unvoiced sound such as <b>/p/, /t/, /k/, /f/</b></td><td><b>/s/</b></td><td><span class="contraction">cup → cups · client → clients · book → books</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>a vowel or a voiced sound, with vibration in your throat</td><td><b>/z/</b></td><td><span class="contraction">key → keys · phone → phones · bag → bags</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>a hissing or buzzing sound such as <b>/s/, /z/, /sh/, /ch/</b></td><td><b>/ɪz/</b>, one extra syllable</td><td><span class="contraction">bus → buses · dish → dishes · watch → watches</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Touch your throat lightly. In <span class="ex">phones</span>, your voice is already vibrating and continues into <span class="ex">/z/</span>. In <span class="ex">clients</span>, the final <span class="ex">/t/</span> has no vibration, so the ending is <span class="ex">/s/</span>. In <span class="ex">buses</span>, add a short extra syllable: <span class="ex">bus-iz</span>.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-lesson-extension="Optional tutor-read plural-ending listening" data-success-message="Correct. Clients and books end in /s/, phones and keys end in /z/, and buses and watches add the extra syllable /ɪz/.">
    <h3>Listen: which ending do you hear?</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Ask your teacher to read the six plural words in order. Choose the final sound before you open the transcript.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Plural ending sound choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="/s/">/s/</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="/z/">/z/</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="/ɪz/" data-value-label-variant="token">/ɪz/ · extra syllable</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>client → plural ending <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="/s/" data-hint="Client ends with the quiet /t/ sound." data-fix="clients ends in /s/" data-placeholder="listen">listen</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>book → plural ending <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="/s/" data-hint="Book ends with the quiet /k/ sound." data-fix="books ends in /s/" data-placeholder="listen">listen</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>phone → plural ending <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="/z/" data-hint="The final /n/ in phone uses your voice." data-fix="phones ends in /z/" data-placeholder="listen">listen</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>key → plural ending <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="/z/" data-hint="Key ends in a vowel sound, so your voice continues." data-fix="keys ends in /z/" data-placeholder="listen">listen</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>bus → plural ending <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="/ɪz/" data-hint="Bus already ends in a hissing /s/ sound, so the plural needs another syllable." data-fix="buses ends in /ɪz/" data-placeholder="listen">listen</button></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>watch → plural ending <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="/ɪz/" data-hint="Watch ends in /ch/, so the plural needs another syllable." data-fix="watches ends in /ɪz/" data-placeholder="listen">listen</button></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    <details>
      <summary>Tutor script and transcript</summary>
      <p>Read naturally, one word at a time: <span class="ex">clients, books, phones, keys, buses, watches</span>. Repeat once in short phrases: <span class="ex">new clients, two books, work phones, house keys, city buses, three watches</span>.</p>
    </details>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Check the spelling decisions</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Is <span class="ex">two box</span> correct? <strong>No.</strong> <span class="ex">box</span> ends in <span class="ex">-x</span>, so we add <span class="ex">-es</span>: <span class="ex">two boxes</span>.</li>
      <li>Is <span class="ex">three citys</span> correct? <strong>No.</strong> <span class="ex">city</span> ends in consonant + y, so drop the y and add <span class="ex">-ies</span>: <span class="ex">three cities</span>.</li>
      <li>Why is it <span class="ex">days</span>, not <span class="ex">daies</span>? Because <span class="ex">day</span> is <strong>vowel + y</strong> (a, e, i, o, u before y). We keep the y and just add <span class="ex">-s</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the plural, then the sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game data-success-message="Correct. Email adds -s, watch adds -es, city changes y to -ies, and key keeps the vowel + y before -s.">
    <h3>Drill 1: match each singular word to its plural</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap a word, then tap the correct plural</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="email">email</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="watch">watch</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="city">city</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="key">key</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="email" data-hint="Email has no special ending, so use the most common pattern." data-fix="email → emails" data-placeholder="emails">emails</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="watch" data-hint="Watch ends in -ch and needs -es." data-fix="watch → watches" data-placeholder="watches">watches</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="city" data-hint="City ends in consonant + y." data-fix="city: drop y, add -ies → cities" data-placeholder="cities">cities</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="key" data-hint="Key ends in vowel + y, so keep the y." data-fix="key + -s → keys" data-placeholder="keys">keys</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. Every number or plural demonstrative is followed by a correctly formed plural noun: meetings, buses, companies, boxes, clients, or days.">
    <h3>Drill 2: choose the correct plural</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">The number in the sentence tells you the noun must be plural</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="meetings">meetings</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="buses">buses</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="companies">companies</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="boxes">boxes</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="clients">clients</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="days">days</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I have three <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="meetings" data-hint="Three requires a plural, and meeting has no special ending." data-fix="three meetings" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> today. <span class="contraction">(meeting + -s)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Two <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="buses" data-hint="Bus ends in -s, so the plural needs -es and an extra syllable." data-fix="two buses" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> stop near the office. <span class="contraction">(bus, ends in -s)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>She works with five <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="companies" data-hint="Company ends in consonant + y, so the y changes." data-fix="five companies" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. <span class="contraction">(company, consonant + y)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>These <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="boxes" data-hint="These is plural, and box ends in -x." data-fix="These boxes are heavy." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> are heavy. <span class="contraction">(box, ends in -x)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>We met four new <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="clients" data-hint="Four requires a plural, and client uses the common -s pattern." data-fix="four new clients" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> this week. <span class="contraction">(client + -s)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The trip is six <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="days" data-hint="Day ends in vowel + y, so keep the y and add -s." data-fix="six days" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> long. <span class="contraction">(day, vowel + y)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="i have three meetings" data-hint="Begin with I have, then place the number before the plural noun." data-fix="I have three meetings." data-success-message="Correct. Three makes meetings plural, and the sentence uses the common -s spelling.">
    <h3>Drill 3: build the sentence</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Three meetings are on your calendar. Build the sentence, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="meetings">meetings</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="three">three</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="have">have</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="these boxes are heavy" data-hint="Begin with the plural demonstrative These, then use are with the plural noun boxes." data-fix="These boxes are heavy." data-success-message="Correct. These, boxes, and are all agree as plural, and box takes -es after -x.">
    <h3>Drill 4: point and describe</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Several boxes are next to you. Build the sentence.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="boxes">boxes</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="these">These</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="heavy">heavy</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="are">are</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="box" data-hint="Two requires a plural noun. Check the noun after two and its final -x." data-fix="I need two boxes for the move." data-why="A word ending in -x adds -es for the plural, so it becomes boxes.">
    <h3>Drill 5: fix the plural</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="need">need</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="two">two</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="box">box</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="citys" data-hint="Three requires a plural. City ends in a consonant followed by y, so check how its final letters change." data-fix="We have offices in three cities." data-why="A consonant before y means the y drops and -ies is added, so it becomes cities.">
    <h3>Drill 6: fix the spelling</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="we">We</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="have">have</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="offices">offices</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="citys">citys.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform data-lesson-extension="Optional no-choice plural transformation">
    <h3>Drill 7: change one to many, then say it</h3>
    <p>Say the plural aloud first. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> one client &nbsp;→&nbsp; two ___</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>two clients</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> one watch &nbsp;→&nbsp; three ___</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>three watches</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> one country &nbsp;→&nbsp; two ___</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>two countries</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> one key &nbsp;→&nbsp; four ___</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>four keys</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> one class &nbsp;→&nbsp; two ___</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>two classes</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your week at work:</b> Say how many of each you have. <span class="ex">I have ___ meetings, ___ emails, and ___ clients this week.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Around your neighborhood:</b> Name plural places near your home. <span class="ex">There are two banks, three offices, and many stores near my home.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Travel plan:</b> Talk about a trip. <span class="ex">I want to visit three cities in two countries. The trip is ___ days.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Around you:</b> Point at real things and count them. <span class="ex">These are my keys. Those are my books. I have two phones.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Quick-fire count:</b> Your teacher says a singular noun, such as <span class="ex">office, dish, day,</span> or <span class="ex">watch</span>. Answer with a number and the correct plural as quickly as possible.</div>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: a one-minute inventory</h3>
    <p>Choose one real area: your workweek, your home, your neighborhood, or a travel plan. Speak for one minute and include at least six plural noun phrases. Your teacher asks one follow-up question. Answer without reading a model.</p>
    <p><b>Success means you:</b></p>
    <ul>
      <li>make the plural meaning clear with a number, <span class="ex">these / those</span>, or another quantity;</li>
      <li>use at least one correct <span class="ex">-s</span>, one <span class="ex">-es</span>, and one consonant + <span class="ex">y → -ies</span> plural;</li>
      <li>keep the y in at least one vowel + y plural, such as <span class="ex">days</span> or <span class="ex">keys</span>;</li>
      <li>make the plural endings audible, including an extra syllable in a word such as <span class="ex">buses</span> or <span class="ex">watches</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the rule</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “After exactly one, I usually use a ______ noun. After zero or a number greater than one, I use a ______ noun. Most regular nouns add ______. After <strong>-s, -x, -z, -ch, -sh</strong> I add ______. After a <strong>consonant + y</strong> I drop the y and add ______. After a <strong>vowel + y</strong> I keep the y and add ______.”</p>
    <p>Then say three true plurals from your real life: one with <span class="ex">-s</span>, one with <span class="ex">-es</span>, and one with <span class="ex">-ies</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Great. You can spell regular plurals with -s, -es, and -ies, and use them with numbers.">
    <h3>Final quiz: choose the correct plural</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="clients" data-hint="Two requires a plural, and client uses the common -s pattern." data-fix="two new clients">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. We met two new ___ today. (client)</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="clients">clients</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="clientes">clientes</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="clienties">clienties</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="watches" data-hint="Watch ends in -ch, so the plural needs -es." data-fix="many watches">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. The store sells many ___. (watch)</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="watchs">watchs</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="watches">watches</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="watchies">watchies</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="cities" data-hint="City ends in consonant + y. Drop the y before adding -ies." data-fix="five cities">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. The company works in five ___. (city)</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="citys">citys</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="cityes">cityes</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="cities">cities</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="days" data-hint="Day ends in vowel + y, so keep the y and add -s." data-fix="ten days">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. The course is ten ___ long. (day)</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="days">days</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="daies">daies</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="dayes">dayes</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="boxes" data-hint="Box ends in -x, so the plural needs -es." data-fix="three boxes">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. Please move these three ___. (box)</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="boxs">boxs</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="boxes">boxes</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="boxies">boxies</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="companies" data-hint="Company ends in consonant + y, so the y changes to -ies." data-fix="Two large companies share the building.">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. Two large ___ share the building. (company)</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="companys">companys</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="companies">companies</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="companyes">companyes</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Two buses are late." data-hint="Bus ends in -s, so add -es. Two also requires are, not is." data-fix="Two buses are late.">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. Which sentence is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Two buses are late.">Two buses are late.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Two buss are late.">Two buss are late.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Two busies are late.">Two busies are late.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="three offices" data-hint="Three requires a plural, and office ends in -s, so add -es." data-fix="three offices">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. Which phrase is correct? (office)</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="three office">three office</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="three offices">three offices</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="three officies">three officies</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check quiz</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset quiz</button>
    </div>
